### 1. PURPOSE AND CONTEXT
This software architecture, codebase, and associated documentation (collectively, the "Software") were developed as part of a Master's Thesis project at Linköping University, in direct collaboration with Scania CV AB (Exhaust Aftertreatment System Development). The Software contains proprietary workflows, parametric logic, and intellectual property explicitly tailored for Scania CV AB's engineering and Product Lifecycle Management (PLM) environment.

